\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{Why records and attempts are distinct}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{replay}
\tag{trajectory-geometry}

\p{A rollout is evidence collected at one point in training. Replay asks
whether that evidence can support another update under a changed policy. The
answer depends on the current policy and therefore belongs to the attempt, not
to the stored record.}

\p{This distinction also separates two recent compute interventions. The DGG
procedure of \citef{miao2026when} reuses a fixed rollout batch until a gradient
diagnostic rejects another update. The NExt procedure of
\citef{chen2026lowrank} predicts a future parameter
displacement from saved checkpoints and then resumes real RL updates. The
first changes the ratio of updates to rollouts. The second replaces part of a
realized parameter path with an extrapolated jump.}

\p{Neither intervention proves that future feedback contains no new
information. A later theorem should charge rejected proposals, stored
checkpoints, predictor fitting, and recovery updates. A no-free-feedback
counterexample should compare environments with identical observed histories
and different later informative events.}
